<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Run the Streamlit app as a background agent on the Mac mini.

  This box is also a Plex server, so the app is deliberately launched under
  macOS background QoS via `taskpolicy -b`. That puts it in the lowest
  scheduling and I/O band, so any Plex transcode always wins contention and the
  app yields instead of competing. Measured cost when idle is a Python process
  with pandas loaded and effectively no CPU; the outcome history it reads builds
  in about a second.

  Bound to 127.0.0.1, because access goes through the Cloudflare tunnel already
  running on this box for the *arr stack. The tunnel connects to localhost, so
  nothing needs to listen on the LAN.

  The app has NO authentication of its own. Every page load acts as your ESPN
  session, so the hostname MUST have a Cloudflare Access policy in front of it.
  A tunnel without Access is a public URL. If you would rather not rely on
  Access, bind 0.0.0.0 instead and reach it over Tailscale, which is not
  publicly routable at all.

  Install:
    cp scripts/com.thecombine.app.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    # edit the two paths below first
    launchctl load -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.thecombine.app.plist
  Check:      launchctl list | grep thecombine
  Stop:       launchctl unload -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.thecombine.app.plist
  Logs:       tail -f <REPO>/logs/app.out

  The CORS and XSRF flags are for running behind a reverse proxy. Streamlit is a
  websocket app, and behind a proxy without them it serves the page and then
  hangs on "Please wait...", which looks like a tunnel problem and is not. They
  are safe here only because Access is doing the authentication.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.thecombine.app</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/taskpolicy</string>
    <string>-b</string>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <!-- REPLACE <REPO> with the absolute path to the checkout, e.g.
         /Users/williamweir/the_combine -->
    <string>cd &lt;REPO&gt; &amp;&amp; exec uv run streamlit run app.py --server.address 127.0.0.1 --server.port 8501 --server.headless true --browser.gatherUsageStats false --server.enableCORS false --server.enableXsrfProtection false</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>&lt;REPO&gt;</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>&lt;REPO&gt;/logs/app.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>&lt;REPO&gt;/logs/app.err</string>

  <!-- Nothing here needs a login session or a GUI. -->
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
